@@ -98,6 +98,16 @@ The following options are provided to configure the output:
 * **`SEPARATOR`**:
     The text string used to set the footnote separator. Defaults to `:`.
 
+* **`USE_DEFINITION_ORDER`**:
+    Whether to number and order the footnotes by the order in which they are
+    defined rather than the order in which they are first referenced in the
+    document. Defaults to `False`.
+
+    By default, footnotes are numbered by the order of their first reference in
+    the document. Footnotes which are only referenced from within other footnotes
+    follow, in the order they are encountered, and footnotes which are never
+    referenced are placed last, in the order in which they are defined.
+
 A trivial example:
 
 ```python
